  m_text: '<align=center><b>Quantum Simulation 3D</b></align>

    <br>A portal
    to a simulation of scaled-up versions of real-world electron and neutron scattering
    experiments, where you can watch particles build up quantum fringe patterns,
    one at a time.

    

    The simulation illustrates how Carolyne Van Vliet''s
    quantum scattering model effectively works. She initially derived William Duane''s
    1923 quantum rule for crystals from modern quantum theory in 1967 and subsequently
    expanded her derivation in 2010 to include the single- and double-slit experiments. '
